views {

  view index {
    title "How to read this — start here"
    description '''
**Colors:** blue = the dispatcher (`bo loop`), purple = worker agents, teal = plan agents, cyan = the Stop hook, amber = gates (only a human closes them), slate = tickets, gray = infrastructure and the human, red dashed = errors that pop up, green = branch worktree boxes.

**Shapes:** person = human, storage = beads DB, cylinder = GitHub, component = dispatcher and hook, agent = worker and planner, rectangle with a lock = gate, document = ticket or note, dashed red rectangle = error.

**Arrows:** dashed gray = blocks (the depends-on chain, read left to right, oldest first), blue = dispatches (one edge per dispatching label), purple = works (agent to ticket), teal dashed = plans (top-down tower build), amber = closes (human to gate), dotted red = raises (where an error pops up).

**The walkthrough order:** 1 plan the tower, 2 one tick of the loop, then the stage views with the branch boxes, then worker to Stop hook to gate, then the epic tier, then every error. A box that repeats across views is the same element, not a copy. Open any node to read its description.
'''
    include dispatcher
    include hook
    include human
    include beads
    include origin
    include decisions
    include planAgents.planEpic
    include workers.engineer
    include workers.testerUnit
    include workers.frontend
    include workers.testerFeature
    include workers.testerE2e
    include workers.reviewAgent
    include workers.mergeAgent
    include tower.featA
    include tower.featA.backendA with { navigateTo stageBackends }
    include errors.labelAmbiguous
    include errors.frontierEmpty
  }

  view towerMap {
    title "Maps / 1. The Tower — the epic, two features, every ticket"
    description '''
**What it is:** the whole beads tower as one linked structure: the epic gate, its three epic tickets, two feature gates each with a five-ticket line — backend-logic, unit-tests, frontend-ui, feature-test, feature-review. Arrows are the depends-on chain; a gate waits on its own review ticket (that edge lives in bd, invisible here — a node may not arrow at its own parent). Open any node to read what is inside the ticket.
'''
    include tower.epic
    include tower.epic.epicMergePr with { navigateTo stageEpicTier }
    include tower.epic.epicE2e with { navigateTo stageEpicTier }
    include tower.epic.epicReview with { navigateTo stageEpicTier }
    include tower.featA
    include tower.featA.backendA with { navigateTo stageBackends }
    include tower.featA.unitA with { navigateTo stageUnits }
    include tower.featA.frontendA with { navigateTo stageFrontends }
    include tower.featA.featureTestA with { navigateTo stageFeatureTier }
    include tower.featA.featureReviewA with { navigateTo stageFeatureTier }
    include tower.featB
    include tower.featB.backendB with { navigateTo stageBackends }
    include tower.featB.unitB with { navigateTo stageUnits }
    include tower.featB.frontendB with { navigateTo stageFrontends }
    include tower.featB.featureTestB with { navigateTo stageFeatureTier }
    include tower.featB.featureReviewB with { navigateTo stageFeatureTier }
  }

  deployment view allBranches {
    title "Maps / 2. Branches — one box per branch"
    description '''
**What it is:** every branch as a container box — `.claude/worktrees/<branch with / to +>`. Inside each box: the worker instances that run there and the tickets whose work lands there. A worktree belongs to a branch, not a ticket: the loop makes it for the branch's first task and every later task re-enters it.
'''
    include worktreesRoot
    include worktreesRoot.wtEpic
    include worktreesRoot.wtA
    include worktreesRoot.wtB
    include worktreesRoot.**
  }

  dynamic view planTower {
    variant sequence
    title "Walkthrough / 1. Plan the tower, top-down"
    description '''
**What it is:** the human and the three plan agents build the whole tower before any work starts. Each plan agent writes exactly one metadata key — its own tier's `branch` — onto its gate and the rows below it.
'''
    human -> planAgents.planEpic "'a recipe box app' — one vague idea"
    planAgents.planEpic -> beads "clarify, research, then create exactly one epic gate + merge / e2e / review tickets" {
      notes 'the only metadata written: { "branch": "epic/recipe-box" } — on the gate and its three tickets'
    }
    human -> planAgents.planFeature "plan the features for RECIPE-1"
    planAgents.planFeature -> beads "RECIPE-5 feature/add-recipe and RECIPE-11 feature/search-recipes, each with feature-test and feature-review" {
      notes 'phased foundations, core, dependent, polish; a colliding sibling gets different words, never -2'
    }
    human -> planAgents.planTask "plan the tasks for RECIPE-5"
    planAgents.planTask -> beads "RECIPE-6, RECIPE-7, RECIPE-8, chained one to the next" {
      notes '''each created labeled: bd create -l backend-logic --parent RECIPE-5
metadata: { "branch": "feature/add-recipe" } copied VERBATIM from the feature gate
every ticket verified with a bd show --json round trip'''
    }
    human -> dispatcher "bo loop — and the tower starts walking itself"
  }

  dynamic view tickWalkthrough {
    variant sequence
    title "Walkthrough / 2. One tick of bo loop"
    description '''
**What it is:** the dispatcher's claim-to-spawn path, with every decision and every error that can pop up on the way. Left-claimed tickets park behind their own lease; unclaimed ones return for the next tick.
'''
    dispatcher -> beads "probe the frontier: bd list --status open,blocked --limit 0" {
      notes 'frontier = [RECIPE-6, RECIPE-12] — the first task of each feature, both unblocked, claimed together'
    }
    dispatcher -> beads "bd ready --claim (atomic — a bare bd ready would let two loops steal the ticket)" {
      notes '''the claim payload:
{"id":"RECIPE-6","labels":["backend-logic"],
 "metadata":{"branch":"feature/add-recipe"},
 "parent":"RECIPE-5"}'''
    }
    alt {
      when 'exactly one dispatching label sits in the AGENT map' {
        dispatcher -> workers.engineer "AGENT[backend-logic] = engineer"
      }
      else 'zero or two dispatching labels' {
        dispatcher -> errors.labelAmbiguous "never guesses a specialist"
        dispatcher -> beads "leave it CLAIMED — the lease parks it off the frontier"
      }
    }
    alt {
      when 'the claim carries metadata.branch' {
        dispatcher -> beads "BO_BRANCH = feature/add-recipe — read off the claim, nothing re-derives it, nothing parses text"
      }
      else 'no branch key in metadata' {
        dispatcher -> errors.metadataMissing "ERROR reason=metadata-missing — left claimed"
      }
    }
    dispatcher -> beads "branchesCurrentlyAtWork()"
    alt {
      when 'another worker already holds feature/add-recipe' {
        dispatcher -> beads "bd unclaim RECIPE-6"
        dispatcher -> errors.branchBusy "one pair of hands per branch; try the next claim, max max_parallel + 2 per tick"
      }
      when 'the branch is free' {
        dispatcher -> tower.epic "walk RECIPE-5 to RECIPE-1 (epicGateOf, two hops at most) — read the PR base off the gate"
      }
    }
    try {
      dispatcher -> origin "ensureEpicGatePr — the gate has no pr: push epic/recipe-box off main, open the PR"
      dispatcher -> beads "bd update RECIPE-1 --set-metadata pr=https://github.com/…/pull/1 (merges — never disturbs branch)"
    } catch {
      dispatcher -> errors.epicPrFailed "left claimed — a worker under a nonexistent epic branch burns a slot; steps: walk, gate-branch, forge, missing-tool, push, pr, annotate"
    }
    dispatcher -> beads "ensureWorktree — git worktree add .claude/worktrees/feature+add-recipe origin/feature/add-recipe"
    alt {
      when 'the worktree cannot be made' {
        dispatcher -> errors.worktreeFailed "ERROR reason=worktree-failed — left claimed"
      }
      when 'the worktree is ready' {
        dispatcher -> workers.engineer "claude --bg --agent engineer --permission-mode bypassPermissions (cwd INSIDE the worktree)" {
          notes '''the six rules the prompt hands the worker — nothing more:
1. keep the lease alive (bd heartbeat)
2. never close your ticket — report in the final message
3. comment what remains
4. spawn nothing
5. stay on your branch; never commit, branch, merge, or push
6. touch $BO_DONE_FILE as the very last action — ONLY if the brief is genuinely complete'''
        }
      }
    }
    alt {
      when 'no session came back' {
        dispatcher -> beads "bd unclaim RECIPE-6"
        dispatcher -> errors.workerNotDispatched "ERROR reason=worker-not-dispatched"
      }
      when 'the worker is live' {
        dispatcher -> beads "log one line, move on — the loop polls nothing, reaps nothing, merges nothing, ends nothing"
      }
    }
  }

  dynamic view workerToGate {
    variant sequence
    title "Walkthrough / 3. Worker, Stop hook, gate"
    description '''
**What it is:** one ticket's life after dispatch — heartbeat, the done marker, the fail-closed Stop hook, and the human closing the gate. The whole safety of the model rests on $BO_DONE_FILE.
'''
    workers.engineer -> beads "bd heartbeat RECIPE-6 — keep the lease alive"
    workers.engineer -> beads "writes src/recipes/validate-recipe.ts in the worktree — never commits, never branches" {
      notes "the work sits uncommitted until the Stop hook files it"
    }
    workers.engineer -> beads "final action: touch $BO_DONE_FILE — only if the brief is genuinely complete" {
      notes "the worker's own declaration; the hook is fail-closed on it"
    }
    hook -> workers.engineer "Stop fires"
    alt {
      when 'no BO_DONE_FILE marker' {
        hook -> errors.notDeclaredDone "ERROR reason=not-declared-done — fail-closed"
        hook -> beads "RECIPE-6 stays claimed; RECIPE-7 chained behind it waits"
      }
      when 'the marker is there' {
        hook -> origin "commit RECIPE-6 onto feature/add-recipe, push, open PR base epic/recipe-box — once per branch, reused after"
        hook -> beads "write metadata pr=… onto RECIPE-6, close the task"
        alt {
          when 'the loop never handed down a target' {
            hook -> errors.noPrTarget "ERROR reason=no-pr-target — named for the target, since pr now means the url"
          }
          when 'BO_PR_TARGET is set' {
            hook -> dispatcher "the line opens one ticket: RECIPE-7 becomes the frontier"
          }
        }
      }
    }
    dispatcher -> workers.testerUnit "AGENT[unit-tests] = tester-unit — respawn means a fresh session of the SAME agent re-checks inside the one ticket"
    workers.testerUnit -> beads "covers every branch of validateRecipe (framework-jest), commits onto feature/add-recipe via the hook"
    workers.reviewAgent -> origin "feature-review: maps entry to exit, trace logs, tests against the instrumented code, findings as PR comments"
    human -> tower.featA "reads the report, verifies the flow, closes RECIPE-5 — only a human closes a gate" {
      notes "its PR merges feature/add-recipe into epic/recipe-box"
    }
    human -> tower.featB "verify, close RECIPE-11"
  }

  dynamic view epicTier {
    variant sequence
    title "Walkthrough / 4. The epic tier assembles"
    description '''
**What it is:** after both feature gates close, the merge assembles the feature branches, the broad tier journeys, the review asks its three questions, and the human closes the epic.
'''
    dispatcher -> workers.mergeAgent "RECIPE-2 epic-merge-pr is on the frontier — dispatched like any other stamp"
    workers.mergeAgent -> origin "read the feature branches off the gates, assemble onto epic/recipe-box, resolve the conflicts, run the tests, report" {
      notes "writes no code, no tests; never merges into main, never opens a PR"
    }
    dispatcher -> workers.testerE2e "RECIPE-3 epic-e2e-test — journeys on the real stack" {
      notes "cross-feature state handoffs, session continuity, one success + one failure journey per feature (framework-playwright)"
    }
    dispatcher -> workers.reviewAgent "RECIPE-4 epic-review — three questions from first principles"
    human -> tower.epic "verify, close the epic gate — thumbs-up on the merged PR into main"
  }

  deployment view stageBackends {
    title "Walkthrough / 5. Stage — back end, two branches at once"
    description '''
**What it is:** the frontier at the tower's bottom tier: RECIPE-6 and RECIPE-12 are each feature's first task, so both are claimed together and the two engineers run side by side — one per branch, never two workers on one branch.
'''
    include worktreesRoot.wtA.engA
    include worktreesRoot.wtA.t_backendA
    include worktreesRoot.wtB.engB
    include worktreesRoot.wtB.t_backendB
  }

  deployment view stageUnits {
    title "Walkthrough / 6. Stage — the micro tier follows its back end"
    description '''
**What it is:** unit-tests waited on the back-end ticket it tests — the line opens one ticket at a time, so tester-unit claims RECIPE-7 only after RECIPE-6 landed. The UI is not built on an unproved function.
'''
    include worktreesRoot.wtA.unitA
    include worktreesRoot.wtA.t_unitA
    include worktreesRoot.wtB.unitB
    include worktreesRoot.wtB.t_unitB
  }

  deployment view stageFrontends {
    title "Walkthrough / 7. Stage — the UI, last in the line"
    description '''
**What it is:** frontend-ui is the last task of the line — built against functions already proved. Its landing unblocks feature-test.
'''
    include worktreesRoot.wtA.feA
    include worktreesRoot.wtA.t_frontA
    include worktreesRoot.wtB.feB
    include worktreesRoot.wtB.t_frontB
  }

  deployment view stageFeatureTier {
    title "Walkthrough / 8. Stage — suite, then review, on the whole feature"
    description '''
**What it is:** nothing is proved against half a feature — feature-test waits on the LAST task, feature-review waits on the suite. Both run on the feature's branch, in their own box.
'''
    include worktreesRoot.wtA.ftA
    include worktreesRoot.wtA.t_ftestA
    include worktreesRoot.wtA.revA
    include worktreesRoot.wtA.t_frevA
    include worktreesRoot.wtB.ftB
    include worktreesRoot.wtB.t_ftestB
    include worktreesRoot.wtB.revB
    include worktreesRoot.wtB.t_frevB
  }

  deployment view stageEpicTier {
    title "Walkthrough / 9. Stage — the epic tier, in its own box"
    description '''
**What it is:** the epic branch's worktree after both gates close: merge assembles, the broad tier journeys, review comments. Then the human closes the epic and the PR into main gets the thumbs-up.
'''
    include worktreesRoot.wtEpic.mergeRun
    include worktreesRoot.wtEpic.e2eRun
    include worktreesRoot.wtEpic.epicReviewRun
    include worktreesRoot.wtEpic.t_merge
    include worktreesRoot.wtEpic.t_e2e
    include worktreesRoot.wtEpic.t_epicReview
  }

  view errorMap {
    title "Walkthrough / 10. Errors that pop up"
    description '''
**What it is:** every alarm the machine can raise, and who raises it. Two dispositions decide everything: LEFT CLAIMED (the lease parks the ticket off the frontier — label-ambiguous, metadata-missing, worktree-failed, epic-pr-failed, not-declared-done) or UNCLAIMED (put straight back for the next tick — worker-not-dispatched, branch-busy). The gray-handled ones are waiting-line probes, not failures: frontier_empty vs tower_stalled is two states of an empty frontier, and only the human can clear a tower stalled behind an open gate.
'''
    include dispatcher
    include hook
    include errors.**
  }
}
